I.2 Session confusion: the failure that injective agreement excludes (Appendix C, Game 3)

```
 Intended binding:   (c, u1, d1)
 Issuer attestation: sigma_I(c, u1, d1, s, n_P, n_I)

 Presented binding:  (c, u2, d2)   with the same sigma_I

 Check performed          Field        Result
 ------------------------ ------------ ---------------------------
 sigma_I verifies         -            PASS  (valid issuer signature)
 credential matches       c            PASS  (same credential)
 nonces fresh             n_P, n_I     PASS  (within window)
 attestation unconsumed   -            PASS  (first presentation)
 account matches          u2 vs u1     NOT CHECKED   <-- break
 device matches           d2 vs d1     NOT CHECKED   <-- break

 Consequence:
   one issuer event  --->  two accepted bindings
   non-injective agreement holds (some event exists)
   injective agreement fails (the event is not unique)
```

Session-table correctness in Game 3 is precisely the property that forbids this: no two distinct accepted tuples map to the same issuer event. The reduction \mathcal{B}_3 is a reduction to that property plus authenticated-channel security, not a reduction to the conclusion.

